      "body": [
        {
          "type": "TextualBody",
          "value": "\n<ol><li dir=\"ltr\">[... and pros]per. By the name of [our Creator]\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">[...] A.M. , t[his] marriage contract was written [...]\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">[... Sut\u016bt] daughter of m(aster) \u1e62ab\u0101\u1e25 (may his) e(nd be) g(ood), and to give her as her mohar and ketubba t[wo] hundred [zuz ...]\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">[...] their wives faithfully. Also she consented and undertook that she\u00a0 ...]\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">[... ser]ve, attend, honor, and esteem their husbands in purity and clea[nness...]\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">[... to] receive the betrothal gift from the hands of Eleazar b. Joseph whose) s(oul is at) r(est). And ...\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">[...] Sut\u016bt, the [v]irgin, the bride, daughter of m(aster) \u1e62ab\u0101\u1e25, (may his) e(nd be) g(ood), with a marriage gift of fi[ve ...]\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">[... wi]th him, alive, and he fulfills her three needs, [she] has no [right\u00a0 \u2026]</li></ol>\n",
